; The child of the secure delegation.  There is nothing wrong with this
; zone in itself: clove signs it properly with a key of its own.  What
; is wrong is that the DS its parent publishes is for some other key, so
; nothing here can be reached from the trust anchor.
$ORIGIN bogus.example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.bogus.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.bogus.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
host	IN	A	192.0.2.9
